keywords:
  - Cayley graph
  - adjacency algebra
  - Jacobson radical
  - real cyclotomic field
  - resultant
  - order
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  The algebra generated by the adjacency matrix of a Cayley graph on a finite abelian group is
  semisimple in characteristic p exactly when every element of the connection set has order prime
  to p. For cycles we find its minimal polynomial in every characteristic and the index of the
  integral algebra in the maximal order, and we show that a prism over an m-cycle has as many
  distinct eigenvalues as an abelian group of order 2m allows if and only if neither 4 nor 6
  divides m. The finite instances are certified in Lean 4.
